description: "Query messaging and voice metrics with SQL: queryMessageMetrics in the TypeScript, Python and Rust clients."
---

`POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/metrics/query`

Runs read-only SQL over the Project's message_events table. Get the SQL schema for supported columns, capabilities, and limits.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.projects.queryMessageMetrics(input: QueryMessageMetricsInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<QueryMessageMetricsOutput>
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Python">
```python Python
photon.projects.query_message_metrics(input: QueryMessageMetricsInput) -> models.QueryMessageMetricsResponse
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Rust">
```rust Rust
client.query_message_metrics(project_id: String, params: Option<QueryMessageMetricsParams>, body: &types::ClickHouseSqlQueryRequest).await -> Result<ResponseValue<types::QueryMessageMetricsResponse>, Error<QueryMessageMetricsError>>
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon({
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.PHOTON_API_TOKEN}` },
});
const result = await photon.projects.queryMessageMetrics({
  path: {
    projectId: "projectId",
  },
  body: {
    sql: "sql",
  },
});
```

```python Python
import os

from photon_api import Photon
from photon_api.rpc_generated import QueryMessageMetricsInput

photon = Photon(headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ['PHOTON_API_TOKEN']}"})
result = photon.projects.query_message_metrics(
    QueryMessageMetricsInput.model_validate({
        "path": {
            "projectId": "projectId",
        },
        "body": {
            "sql": "sql",
        },
    })
)
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::{Credential, PhotonClientBuilder, SecretString};

let token = std::env::var("PHOTON_API_TOKEN")?;
let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new()
    .credential("accountServiceKey", Credential::Bearer(SecretString::from(token)))
    .build()?;
let result = client
    .query_message_metrics(
        "projectId".to_owned(),
        None,
        &serde_json::from_value(serde_json::json!({
            "sql": "sql",
        }))?,
    )
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

